  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A shell stitch baby blanket is 75 x 90 cm. Rows of five-treble "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "shell-stitch"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "shells"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " sit over the spaces from the previous row. The result is a light, open fabric in DK cotton on a 4 mm hook."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each shell repeat is 6 stitches wide plus one chain. At this gauge a 75 cm blanket needs 12 shell repeats across. The pattern is one row to learn and then repeats to the end. Total yardage is around 300 g."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "DK cotton yarn",
              "qty": "300 g"
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "5 shells x 8 rows = 10 x 10 cm in DK cotton with a 4 mm hook. Work one row of shells and measure 5 across. A half-shell difference per 10 cm shifts the finished width by 3 cm over 75 cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "ch: chain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "dc (UK) / sc (US): double crochet (edge stitch)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "shell: 5 tr into the same stitch or space"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Foundation chain"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chain 148 (12 repeats of 12 ch + 4 edge ch)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 1 (right side)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "turning-chain"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Turning chain"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " of ch 3. *Skip 2 ch. Work 5 tr into next ch (shell made). Skip 2 ch. Work 1 dc into next ch. Ch 1*. Repeat to end, ending with 5 tr into last repeat, dc into last ch. Turn. (12 shells.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 2 and onward"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 3. *Work 1 shell into the centre tr of each shell. Work 1 dc into each ch-1 space*. Repeat. Turn. (12 shells.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Repeat Row 2 until piece measures 90 cm (about 72 rows). Fasten off."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Edging"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work one round of dc (UK) around the perimeter. Work 1 dc into each stitch on top and bottom. Work 1 dc into each row end on the sides. Work 3 dc into each corner."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Secure tails with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "weaving-in-ends"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "weaving in ends"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Block lightly with steam to open the shells."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash 30 degrees gentle. Dry flat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The v-stitch blanket uses a two-treble fan for a more open look. Or try the bobble blanket for raised texture in the same DK cotton."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}